>
  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Summary:</strong> OpenPub collects no data. Your files are opened and converted on your Mac, and nothing is sent to us or anyone else.
  </div>

  <h2>What It Collects</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing. There is no account, no analytics, no advertising and no tracking. The app has no network access, so it cannot upload your files.
  </p>

  <h2>What Stays on Your Mac</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your files.</strong> OpenPub reads only the .pub files you open or drop on it, and writes PDF or PNG files only where you choose to save them.</li>
    <li><strong>Previews.</strong> The Quick Look and thumbnail extensions render .pub files on your Mac when Finder asks for a preview.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Purchases</h2>
  <p>
    The one-time unlock is sold through the App Store. Apple handles the payment; we never see your payment details or Apple Account.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions: <a href="mailto:matt@mattdonders.com">matt@mattdonders.com</a></p>
</DocLayout>
